Since $1\text{ kilogram}=1000\text{ grams}$, we know that both $\dfrac{1\text{ kilogram}}{1000\text{ grams}}$ and $\dfrac{1000\text{ grams}}{1\text{ kilogram}}$ equal $1$.

So we can multiply by either of those fractions to help us convert units, since multiplying by $1$ doesn't change value. In this problem, we multiply by $\blueD{\dfrac{1\text{ kilogram}}{1000\text{ grams}}}$ since the quantity we want to convert is in $\text{grams}$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}80\,\cancel{\text{grams}}\cdot \blueD{\dfrac{1\text{ kilogram}}{1000\,\,\cancel{\text{grams}}}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{80}{1000}\,\text{kilograms}
\end{align}$
